    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nFor similar groups of command, I use the same description prefix.\nSorting by description makes it easier for me to search the command I am looking for, then press the correct key.\n(I don't use mini.clue to discover new keymap, in this case, keymap sorting might be more intuitive).\n\n\nBefore:\n<img width=\"394\" height=\"520\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2f13ff92-2fa8-429c-981a-013564323499\" />\nAfter:\n<img width=\"392\" height=\"334\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/df443e97-6645-4389-9c16-1b2cce94678b\" />\n\nMy hacky patch:\n```patch\ndiff --git i/lua/mini/clue.lua w/lua/mini/clue.lua\nindex 232311c..4681dd2 100644\n--- i/lua/mini/clue.lua\n+++ w/lua/mini/clue.lua\n@@ -1873,6 +1873,8 @@ H.clues_to_buffer_content = function(clues, keys)\n     table.insert(res, { next_key = next_key, desc = desc, is_group = is_group, has_postkeys = data.has_postkeys })\n   end\n \n+  table.sort(res, function(a, b) return a.desc < b.desc end)\n+\n   return res\n end\n ```\n\nMade into my lazy config:\n```\n  build = [[\nsed -i '/table.insert(res, { next_key/ {n; n; a\\\ntable.sort(res, function(a, b) return a.desc < b.desc end)\n}' lua/mini/clue.lua\n  ]], -- HACK: sort clues alphabetically\n```",
